  "summary": "Rock sills stabilize sediment in the Maurice River Estuary, supporting salt-marsh restoration, wildlife habitat, recreation, and natural flood defense.",
  "storyTitle": "Project narrative",
  "description": [
    "The design aims to restore New Jersey’s Maurice estuary salt marshes by using rock sills to stabilize sediment and create habitats for native plants and wildlife. This low-energy area will enhance sediment accumulation, promoting a resurgence of essential ecosystems. The project not only supports biodiversity, including migratory birds, but also provides recreational opportunities and natural flood defense, embodying a holistic approach to coastal and environmental resilience."
  ],
